REA Studio hosted browser acceptance proposal â€” 2026-10-15

Status: source inspection and design only. No browser, product, build or test was executed locally. No active application, test, dependency or workflow source was edited for this proposal.

Current evidence and gap

The completed Flow/Vault PR run38808919004 tested merge7d5bde3fb94e3383e6d85e50e7d567516cc6202c on GitHub-hosted windows-2022, Node24.16.0. Its49 current test files passed282 checks with zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo and768 stable eligible census files;346 active snapshots were captured. The four separate synthetic failure controls failed closed as intended. The full portable artifact, logs and verified readable contents are backed up locally. Those results are not a browser result.

Current package.json has no browser test dependency or browser command. Current Flow link-ui-fixture.mjs supplies a custom Element implementation with modeled geometry and event dispatch. normalization-ui.test.mjs explicitly records actualBrowserExecutions=0 and observes Blob contents without a real browser download. Native textarea normalization, actual uploaded/downloaded bytes, real SVG pointer capture/layout and navigation disposal therefore remain material browser acceptance targets. Vault UI tests similarly use fixture DOM objects. Historical browser records remain historical and are not rebound by the proposed run.

The unchanged products/rea-studio/server.mjs exports start({port:0,dataDir}) and returns its actual loopback URL, token and close(). It binds127.0.0.1, serves the real studio and client ES modules, creates all ten application contexts and enforces the actual token-gated API. This is sufficient to run a browser in the same hosted Windows job; no public deployment, tunnel, paid service, vendor acquisition or local service is needed. The current public/studio.mjs generates the navigation and imports real app clients.

Proposed separate implementation

1. Add an isolated browser-tools package and lockfile, separate from application package.json, plus *.spec.mjs acceptance files so existing *.test.mjs Node discovery is unchanged. Pin @playwright/test1.64.1 and its exact playwright1.64.1 dependency; the official npm registry metadata read2026-10-15 reports Node>=20 and integrity sha512-IaYGml/nSOiZWROfPtuIL7neuu9qDOZ3TNvNljUIrhDMxiGTgPjzj/g9p9RxpS2tSepPDRY+UwAaEeiKtUvIAg==. Generate and commit the lock through a hosted source-preparation step; do not use an unpinned npx download. Authenticate the package-lock identity in the browser attempt receipt.

2. Use one standard GitHub-hosted windows-2022 job with exact Node24.16.0 and the already verified full-SHA checkout/setup-node/upload-artifact pins. Start with manual dispatch and relevant PR paths/main pushes; avoid duplicate branch-push runs. npm ci installs only the locked test tools; invoke that installed Playwright CLI to install its matching Chromium revision. Keep browser downloads in RUNNER_TEMP and out of artifacts/Git. Record package versions, browser.version(), browser executable identity, runner image metadata and same SHA/run/attempt/repository binding. This is an actual Chromium browser, initially one browser/desktop viewport only. Wider browser/device acceptance is separate.

3. A hosted-only bounded collector owns the server fixture and browser runner. It imports the committed server start() with port0 and an exclusive RUNNER_TEMP synthetic-data directory, receives the actual URL, starts the tests and closes only its owned browser/server/data handles. It must not reuse an existing listener. No source overlays are needed for Flow/Vault browser acceptance. Capture an explicit source manifest for runtime, browser harness/config/lock and current test fixtures before execution, and require identical bytes afterward. Preserve a running then terminal receipt and streaming raw logs even after failures; use one worker, zero retries, an8-minute browser global deadline and15-minute job deadline. Missing browser, skipped test, flaky/retried result, page crash, unexpected console/page error, source mutation or incomplete child close fails the acceptance gate.

Finite initial matrix (proposed, not executed)

All ten applications: navigate through actual visible navigation buttons; verify heading, rendered client root and expected empty-state/control; capture console/page errors and failed first-party requests. This is ten-app navigation smoke coverage, not complete ten-app browser acceptance.

Flow:
- Upload owned JSON containing CRLF, bareCR, LF, U+2028, astral and combining Unicode; observe the real textarea's normalized display; Save/Deploy/Export through real UI; read browser download bytes and real API persisted raw text to prove backing text retains only the intended normalization behavior.
- Make a genuine dirty edit; clicking Deploy must keep the draft and refuse before a native-deploy API request. Renaming an otherwise unchanged saved draft must retain exact imported raw bytes.
- Load the static Link In/Out scene, inspect the rendered dashed virtual edge and suppressed overwritten wire, then Disconnect/Connect/Save/Deploy/Inject through actual controls; verify retained opaque metadata and resulting debug destinations through the real API.
- Drag an SVG node with actual pointer events and measured browser geometry. Check coordinate change, existing metadata preservation and no mutation when the pending-action guard applies.
- Hold one real response after route.fetch() has executed the unchanged host handler; keep its original status/headers/body, without mocking handler output. Type a newer draft while the real Save or validation response is held, release it and assert newer draft retention, duplicate-button gating and the exact persisted submitted source. Record the hold as an explicit network-timing fault, separate from ordinary UI checks.
- Navigate away while a real response is held, then release it. Confirm no stale publication, detached control scrubbing and correct freshly loaded state when returning.

Vault (synthetic master password and entries only):
- Create an encrypted vault through UI; create a parent/child group and edit details. Confirm the expected UI grouping and actual persisted values after page reload.
- Hold a committed groupCreate response, type a newer group name/notes, release, and verify conversion to Save group details retains the newer draft and the submitted group is created exactly once. A later explicit Save updates that same ID.
- Repeat the newer-draft test for groupSave; verify persisted submitted values and retained newer controls separately, then explicit final save.
- Dirty entry/group drafts must prevent conflicting group/entry actions until Save or explicit discard; verify zero disallowed transport calls. Confirm/discard controls must use real DOM inputs.
- Navigate away or Lock while group/entry work is pending; release original real response and verify detached secrets are scrubbed and stale panels do not reopen. Keep synthetic visible-password checks separate from actual cryptographic interoperability, which belongs to the existing original-comparison suites.

Evidence and gate

Use a new rea-cloud-browser-attempt/v1 receipt with status running/passed/failed/interrupted, explicit finite scenario roster, real browser and source identity, source-before/source-after hashes, request/result observations, all-zero skipped/fail/retry totals, console/page errors and child close status. Save a small semantic JSON result, raw text logs, exact uploaded/downloaded fixture fingerprints and selected PNG screenshots. Screenshot files are observations, not automatic pixel-baseline approval. Disable video; retain a bounded trace on failure only. Use the existing15MiB compressed cap and1-day retention, fail visibly with an explicitly incomplete compact fallback if exceeded, then download and verify the actual portable artifact locally. No vendor/browser binaries, real user data or host environment dump enter the artifact.

Accept only successful same-attempt browser receipt, source postcheck, workflow conclusion and locally readable complete evidence together. Keep ten-app navigation smoke, finite Flow/Vault browser acceptance, broader browser coverage, full development contracts, original comparisons, production security and feature/performance superiority as separate claims. No new browser success exists yet.

Primary documentation consulted (read only)

https://playwright.dev/docs/intro â€” official platform/Node support and browser capabilities.
https://playwright.dev/docs/ci â€” official CI installation, one-worker recommendation and bounded global timeout before the job limit.
https://playwright.dev/docs/test-webserver â€” server lifecycle/readiness/reuse controls. An owned start({port:0}) wrapper avoids fixed-port collision and permits explicit close in this repository.
https://playwright.dev/docs/trace-viewer-intro â€” portable trace evidence.
https://registry.npmjs.org/@playwright%2ftest/latest â€” observed exact1.64.1 metadata/integrity; execution must use the committed exact lock rather than latest.

