Observed official tooling metadata

Official npm registry responses were fetched read-only and preserved as actual UTF-8 contents in provenance/packages/{playwright-test,playwright,playwright-core}.json. All three exact versions are1.64.1. Their real official tarball URLs and SHA512 integrity values are copied into the candidate lock and asserted by the collector. No tarball/package/vendor/browser binary was downloaded locally and no npm command was executed locally. This small v3 lock was source-authored from the complete three-package dependency closure; hosted npm ci --include=dev --ignore-scripts is the required actual validation.

Official Microsoft Playwright Git ref v1.64.1 resolved through the public GitHub API to commit cfe490d941f992655948eee8fd4fd94e1c4234bf. Its actual packages/playwright-core/browsers.json is preserved in provenance/browsers.json and byte-copied to candidate browser-metadata.json:1135bytes, SHA2562cfd419f71ac6475d81e1301fa86c34cf2a2a6bae2a0da4b5a2b18310216b6bf. It declares Chromium revision1248/version156.0.8078.4. The hosted collector requires installed playwright-core/browsers.json to equal these bytes before acquisition. It invokes the installed pinned CLI with install chromium --no-shell, then the configuration uses channel chromium for the full browser's new headless mode. The actual executable byte count/SHA256 are observed only on the hosted runner; no publisher binary digest, binary signature, historical equivalence or local browser launch is invented.

